.Dt MBT_BE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_be_value_parse ,
.Nm mbt_be_value_encode ,
.Nm mbt_be_ref ,
.Nm mbt_be_unref ,
.Nm mbt_be_unrefp ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append_number ,
.Nm mbt_be_dict_append_string ,
.Nm mbt_be_list_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_list_append ,
.Nm mbt_be_string_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_integer_new ,
.Nm mbt_be_find ,
.Nm mbt_be_walk ,
.Nm mbt_be_pp
.Nd Bencode parsing and construction library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/be.h
.Fn mbt_be_value_parse "const unsigned char *buf" "size_t sz" "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_value_encode "struct mbt_be_value *v" "unsigned char **out" "size_t *len"
.Ft "struct mbt_be_value *"
.Fn mbt_be_ref "struct mbt_be_value *v"
.Ft "struct mbt_be_value *"
.Fn mbt_be_unref "struct mbt_be_value *v"
.Fn mbt_be_unrefp "struct mbt_be_value **v"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_new "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "struct mbt_be_value *value"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append_number "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "int64_t num"
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append_string "struct mbt_be_value *dict" "char *key" "const void *buf" "size_t len"
.Fn mbt_be_list_new "struct mbt_be_value **out"
.Fn mbt_be_list_append "struct mbt_be_value *list" "struct mbt_be_value *val"
.Fn mbt_be_string_new "struct mbt_be_value **out" "const void *buf" "size_t len"
.Fn mbt_be_integer_new "struct mbt_be_value **out" "int64_t val"
.Fn mbt_be_find "struct mbt_be_value *be" "const char *key"
.Fn mbt_be_walk "struct mbt_be_value *be" "int (*cb)(struct mbt_be_value *, void *)" "void *arg"
.Fn mbt_be_pp "struct mbt_be_value *be" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_be
library provides utilities for parsing, constructing, and traversing
bencoded data structures. Bencoding is the serialization format used by
the BitTorrent protocol.
.Pp
All operations revolve around the
.Vt mbt_be_value
structure, which can represent a string, an integer, a list, or a
dictionary.
.Sh PARSING AND ENCODING
.Fn mbt_be_value_parse
takes a buffer of bencoded bytes and produces a tree of
.Vt mbt_be_value
structures.
.Fn mbt_be_value_encode
encodes a tree of
.Vt mbt_be_value
structures back into a dynamically allocated buffer of bencoded bytes.
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned buffer.
.Pp
.Vt mbt_be_value
objects are reference counted.
.Fn mbt_be_ref
increments the reference count and returns the same pointer.
.Fn mbt_be_unref
decrements the reference count; when it reaches zero the object and all
its children are freed.
It always returns
.Dv NULL ,
which is useful for clearing a pointer in one expression.
.Fn mbt_be_unrefp
is a
.Fn cleanup
wrapper suitable for use with
.Dv _cleanup_be_ :
.Bd -literal
_cleanup_be_ struct mbt_be_value *msg = NULL, *m = NULL;
if (mbt_be_dict_new(&msg) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
if (mbt_be_dict_new(&m) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
if (mbt_be_dict_append_number(m, "ut_pex", 4) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
if (mbt_be_dict_append(msg, "m", m) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
/* both msg and m are freed automatically; no = NULL needed after append */
.Ed
.Sh CONSTRUCTION
To create bencoded data, use the following factory functions:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_new
Creates a new empty dictionary.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_list_new
Creates a new empty list.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_string_new
Creates a new string value from an existing buffer of bytes.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_integer_new
Creates a new integer value.
.El
.Pp
Once structures are created, they can be populated:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_append
Appends a previously created
.Vt mbt_be_value
to a dictionary under the given key.
The dictionary increments the reference count of
.Fa value ,
so the caller retains its own reference and need not null out the pointer.
When the caller holds a
.Dv _cleanup_be_
variable, no
.Dv = NULL
is required after the append.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_dict_append_number
Appends an integer value to a dictionary with the given key.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It Fn mbt_be_dict_append_string
Appends raw bytes as a string to a dictionary with the given key.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_be_list_append
Adds a value to the end of a list.
The list increments the reference count of
.Fa val ;
the caller retains its own reference.
.El
.Sh TRAVERSAL AND INSPECTION
.Fn mbt_be_find
searches for a key within a dictionary and returns the associated
.Vt mbt_be_value. Returns
.Fa NULL
if the key is not found.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_be_walk
performs a depth-first traversal of the bencoded structure, invoking a
callback function for every node encountered.
.Pp
The following functions are for debugging or utility:
.Fn mbt_be_pp
pretty-prints the bencoded structure (e.g., to a file or stdout via an argument).
.Fn mbt_be_streq
(inline) checks if a bencoded string node contains the exact bytes of a
provided C string.
.Sh OWNERSHIP
.Fn mbt_be_dict_append
transfers ownership of
.Fa value
to the dictionary.
The caller must set their reference to
.Dv NULL
after a successful append to avoid a double-free when the parent is
released:
.Bd -literal
_cleanup_be_ struct mbt_be_value *a = NULL;
if (mbt_be_dict_new(&a) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
/* populate a ... */
if (mbt_be_dict_append(msg, "a", a) < 0) return -ENOMEM;
a = NULL; /* transferred */
.Ed
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Construction functions return 0 on success or
.Er -ENOMEM
on allocation failure.
Parsing functions return the number of bytes consumed on success, or a
negative error code on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Constructing a simple dictionary with automatic cleanup:
.Bd -literal
_cleanup_be_ struct mbt_be_value *dict = NULL;
if (mbt_be_dict_new(&dict) < 0)
    return -ENOMEM;
if (mbt_be_dict_append_number(dict, "length", 1024) < 0)
    return -ENOMEM;
if (mbt_be_dict_append_string(dict, "name", "my_torrent", 10) < 0)
    return -ENOMEM;
unsigned char *buf;
size_t len;
mbt_be_value_encode(dict, &buf, &len);
/* use buf ... */
free(buf);
/* dict freed automatically on return */
.Ed
